- For fine-tuning strategy, the highest validation accuracies are achieved with masking ratios between 50% and 80%. Specifically, masking ratios of 60%, 70%, and 75% all result in validation accuracies of 84.9% or higher, suggesting that these intermediate to high masking ratios are beneficial for learning rich representations.
- For linear probing, the trend is less clear due to fewer trials, but it appears that higher masking ratios (up to 80%) yield better results than very low masking ratios.

